# English UI — NeoSaaS

NeoSaaS product copy is **English only**. Do not introduce French (or other) user-visible strings in the application.

## Always English

- Sidebar / header navigation labels and group titles
- Page headings (`<h1>`) and browser tab titles (`usePageTitle` from `@/hooks/use-page-title`)
- Buttons, toasts, dialogs, placeholders, empty states, loading text
- Admin guards and access-denied messages
- `lib/search-catalog.ts` entries for new routes
- API `error` / `message` fields consumed by the UI

## Client dashboard titles (align menu ↔ page)

| Route | Title |
|-------|-------|
| `/dashboard` | Catalog |
| `/dashboard/company-management` | Company Management |
| `/dashboard/payments` | Payments |
| `/dashboard/profile` | Profile |
| `/dashboard/chat` | Chat |
| `/dashboard/support` | Support |

Account footer menu: collapsible **Account** → **Profile** (Company Management, Payments) + **Support** (Chat, Support).

## Implementation

```tsx
usePageTitle("Payments") // browser tab
<h1 className="text-3xl font-bold">Payments</h1> // must match menu
```

Use `en-US` for dates/numbers shown to users.

## Do not

- Add French menu items (e.g. "Catalogue", "Gestion de compte") without an i18n system
- Ship French toasts, guards, or placeholders
- Mix languages on the same screen

Full policy: `docs/LANGUAGE.md`
